    core_synastry: `When one chart's Vesta meets another's Sun at opposition, the Vesta-bearer's need for devotion and the Sun-bearer's drive toward broad identity face each other across the full width of the synastry axis. What the Vesta-bearer wants as sustained dedication sits at one pole; what the Sun-bearer wants to express broadly sits at the other. Both are entirely visible to the other. The geometry produces a bond where focus and breadth are in constant encounter across difference.`,
    behavioral_synastry: `The Vesta-bearer often becomes the person who dedicates with sustained focus, and the Sun-bearer often becomes the person who maintains broad autonomous purpose. The two chart-bearers hold opposite ends of the same axis for each other. Done consciously, this produces a bond where each person witnesses what the other cannot fully access. Done unconsciously, it produces a relationship where the Vesta-bearer feels they are always the one narrowing to devotion and the Sun-bearer feels they must always protect breadth.`,
    friendship_synastry: `In a friendship, this opposition produces a bond where the two friends represent different relationships to dedication and breadth. The Vesta-bearer may be further along in sustained focus; the Sun-bearer may be further along in maintaining wide purpose. The friendship works when both people can learn from the pole the other embodies.`,
